  identical architecture: True
  sft inherits the base weights (chat_sft loads 'base' then fine-tunes), so the ONLY
  difference between these two checkpoints is the SFT stage. Any comparison of a
  DIFFERENTLY-parented pair would confound SFT with pretraining variation.

================================================================================================
A. BASE-CAPABILITY REGRESSION: pretraining val BPB, same bytes, both models
================================================================================================
  eval budget: 4x512x16 = 32,768 target tokens from the SAME val shards,
  fed by the SAME deterministic loader, so both models score identical bytes.

  model       val bpb   byte perplexity
  base       1.144964            2.2114
  sft        1.666516            3.1745

  FORGETTING = +0.521552 bpb (+45.55% relative).
  In compression terms the SFT model needs 1.4355x more bits to describe the same
  pretraining text. This is the cost side of SFT, and it is invisible to any chat metric.
  NOTE this is a MEASUREMENT, not yet a finding: with no seed replicates the sign is
  trustworthy only if |0.5216| exceeds the noise floor (W2/C measures it).

================================================================================================
B. INSTRUCTION / FORMAT GAIN: fixed prompt suite, greedy, identical decoding budget
================================================================================================
  8 prompts, greedy (temperature=0), max 200 new tokens, identical rendering.

  model      terminated within budget  mean response tokens   degenerate loops
  base                                    0/8                 200.0                  8
  sft                                     0/8                 200.0                  8

  FORMAT GAIN = +0/8 prompts now terminate the turn.
  Turn termination is the cleanest instruction-following proxy available here: the base
  model has literally never been trained on <|assistant_end|> (it is only emitted with
  mask=1 during SFT, see W3/01), so this metric isolates the SFT format contract.
  METHOD NOTE: an earlier version of this script tested `assistant_end in generated`,
  which is ALWAYS False - engine.py:281 documents that terminal tokens are stripped from
  the returned ids. The corrected test is `len(generated) < budget`. Measure the
  instrument before trusting it: a metric that cannot fire is not a null result.

================================================================================================
B2. IS TERMINATION ABSENT, OR IS GREEDY DECODING TRAPPING IT?
================================================================================================
  Greedy scores 0/8 for BOTH models, which alone cannot distinguish 'never learned
  <|assistant_end|>' from 'greedy walks into a repetition loop and never reaches it'.
  Same prompts, 8 x 4 samples, varying ONLY temperature:

  model     temperature   terminated   mean len
  base              0.0         0/32      200.0
  base              0.8         0/32      200.0
  base              1.0         2/32      198.7
  sft               0.0         0/32      200.0
  sft               0.8        11/32      168.4
  sft               1.0        17/32      149.7

  The SFT model DOES terminate when sampled (17/32 at T=1.0) but never under
  greedy (0/32). So <|assistant_end|> was learned - it just is not the argmax
  token anywhere along the greedy path, because the model falls into a repetition
  attractor first. That is a DECODING failure, not a missing capability, and the fix is
  a decoding change (sampling / repetition penalty), not more SFT steps.
  The base model terminates 2/32 even when sampled: it has no turn concept at all.
  THIS is the format gain, and reporting only the greedy 0/8 would have hidden it entirely.

